1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DEATHS Mrs. Henry Heinze. Mrs. Henry Heinze, an old and much respected resident of this vicinity, died suddenly at her home in the First ward yesterday afternoon at 4:30 of apoplexy. Mrs. Heinze was a native of Sax
2 CONC ony, Germany born 74 years ago; her maiden name was Catherine Scharf. She came to America with her husband in the early 80's and has since made her home in Columbia county: the past eight years she has resided in Portage with her 
2 CONC husband. She was a devout Christian woman and a consistant [et. al.] member of the Lutheran church. Last February Mr. and Mrs. Heinze observed their golden wedding anniversary. Besides her husband she leaves five children; they ar
2 CONC e Mrs. Aug. Kopplin of Caledonia; Louis W. Heinze of Dekorra. She leaves one sister, Mrs. Ernest Heinze of Lewiston, and a brother, Albert Scharf of Summit S. D. The funeral will be held from the residence Tuesday morning at 11 o'
2 CONC clock, Rev. Haeuser officiating.
